      "customfield_10001" : "1_*:*_1_*:*_81868184582_*|*_5_*:*_1_*:*_0",
      "customfield_10012" : "0|i003wv:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "e.g. want:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "static constexpr TimeOfDay kMin {0};",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Doing that inside struct TimeOfDay fails cuz TimeOfDay is incomplete at that point so cannot be declared literaltype.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "From what I saw in various docs - that seems wrong - but clang/gcc/msvc all agreee.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "I should also be able to do const inside the static declaration, and then use constpr as definition. This works so long as I only put the constexpr guy in one file. BUt attempting to add to a second gets duplicate defs error (warning on windows, error on unix).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "https://wandbox.org/"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "https://wandbox.org/",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "seems to work…",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "struct A {",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "int f;",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "constexpr A () : f (0) {}",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "constexpr A (int i) : f ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "attrs" : {
                        "id" : "atlassian-info",
                        "shortName" : ":info:",
                        "text" : ":info"
                     },
                     "type" : "emoji"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : " {}",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "//static constexpr A kMin {3};\t// doesn’t work cuz compiler says A incomplete type",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "static const A kMin;",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "};\t",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "constexpr A A:: kMin {3};\t// but then generates link errors  - dup defined",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "I realized template std::numeric_limits has this same issue - I'm trying todo. But it uses functions:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "T numeric_limits<T>::max ().",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "So I used that pattern.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Note here that if I can find a way around this, then it would be better to go back to kMax/kMin instead of min()/max() functions. But this is functional, and OK for now. easy on any compiler etc.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
